          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.4 Attraction and Repulsion between Magnets"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.127,
            0.591,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 4.5: Let us experiment"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.159,
            0.883,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take a pair of bar magnets on which North and South poles have been marked. Mark the two bar magnets as A and B."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.221,
            0.882,
            0.263
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Place the longer side of magnet A over 5–6 round shaped pencils as shown in Fig. 4.8a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.266,
            0.883,
            0.326
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now bring one end of magnet B near the end of magnet A placed on the pencils. Make sure that the two magnets do not touch each other. Observe what happens."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.329,
            0.885,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Next, bring the other end of magnet B near the same end of magnet A (Fig. 4.8b). Does the magnet A on the pencils begin to move? Does it always move in the direction of the approaching magnet? What do these observations suggest?"
            }
          ]
        },
